      "content": "a\nt = +1.5\nt = +1.5\nt = 0\nt = 0\nt = -1.5\nt = -1.5\nb\nc\nt = +1.5\nt = 0\nt = -1.5\nFIG. 3. Time evolution of magnetic ﬁeld lines and energy density for a: the trefoil knot (p = 2, q = 3), b: the cinquefoil knot (p = 2, q = 5)\nand c: the 4 Hopf-linked rings (p = 2, q = 2). Shown is the topology preserving, ﬂuid-like evolution of the core ﬁeld line(s) (orange), and ﬁeld\nline(s) (blue) lying on tori (purple) enclosing the core.\nwhere g = gcd(p, q), k ∈{0, 1, . . . , g −1} and θ ∈[0, 2π)\nparametrizes the curve(s). The curves K±\nB lie on a torus, wind-\ning p times in the toroidal direction and q times i",
